WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.290
Speaker 1: There has been speculation and
questions as to whether Joe Biden will run

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.040
for reelection in 2024.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:13.269
Now you already you may know my position on
this already, and my position on this is that

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:21.460
I see a Joe Biden reelection as a very tough
uphill battle, and I see a Kamala Harris replacement

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:27.349
of Joe Biden as the Democratic nominee in
2024 as a very tough uphill battle.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:31.470
Now sometimes people will write to me and
they'll say, David, are you saying that so

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.520
that people don't rest on their laurels and
tune out?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.620
Or are you saying that?

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.340
Are you overstating that or I'm not gaming
anything.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.190
I am just giving my honest opinion, my genuine
opinion.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.480
It doesn't mean I have someone I think would
do.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.350
I have no, I have.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.120
There's no superstar right now in the Democratic
Party that I love and I feel super inspired

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.120
by.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.230
I don't have any better alternatives at this
point to Biden and Harris.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:05.320
I'm just saying I see the reelection hill
as a very steep one for both Joe Biden and

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.610
Kamala Harris.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:13.810
The White House has put out a statement saying
Joe Biden intends to run in 2024, and this

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.170
created so many headlines of people saying
he's running.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.170
He's running.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.740
And I think you have to understand that there
is one important word in this headline and

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.780
that word is intense.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.470
It is intense.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:32.560
And what one intends to do in 2021, 10 months
into their presidency can have absolutely

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:38.090
no connection whatsoever to what one actually
does in 2024.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:43.040
CNN summarizing the article, saying the White
House said on Monday that Joe Biden intends

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.830
to run for reelection in 2024, following a
recent report indicating that the commander

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:53.670
in chief and staff are attempting to assuage
concerns about his future political prospects.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.890
When White House press secretary Jen Psaki
was asked aboard Air Force One whether she

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:03.760
could confirm if he was going to run in 2024
and whether he was telling staff that she

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.470
responded Yes, that's his intention.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.840
The Washington Post reported Biden and members
of his inner circle have been telling.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.310
Allies, he plans to run again and attempt
to address concerns about whether he could

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.459
commit to another presidential campaign given
his age.

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:24.400
A recent Quinnipiac poll showed Biden's approval
rating sits at 36 percent now.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:31.740
Very important to remember that if you actually
look at the FiveThirtyEight Biden approval,

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.260
it's actually not much changed from where
it was.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:39.930
It's still at 43 percent and it's been there
basically going all the way back to a month

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:40.930
ago.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:46.300
So although it is true that there is a Quinnipiac
poll showing Biden at 36, on average, there's

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.849
been no movement for a month or maybe even
like five or six weeks.

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:54.510
That doesn't mean Biden's approval rating
is particularly good right now.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:03:00.850
But the 36 percent number is very much an
outlier, so this entire story is about the

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.069
word intense.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:09.500
Intense can have a very different meaning
if things change or if whatever happens.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:16.540
If you said today, David, sir, even money
bet no odds, just if you all you have to bet

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.209
on is, does Biden run or does Biden not run?

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:25.470
I would take the even money bet on Biden does
not run for reelection.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.770
It's not by much.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:29.349
Right now, I would say I'm.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:36.870
55, 45, maybe 60, 40 that Joe Biden does not
run for reelection in 2024.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.510
We don't know, too.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.810
I know people were right, will write in and
say, David, you're wrong.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:49.380
It's an odds prediction for which a marginally
feel more confident that Biden doesn't run.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.099
It's not like a big claim.

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:53.959
I'm not saying that it's a statement of fact.

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:56.900
It's a statement of opinion because it's in
the future.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:03.599
And I'm saying 55, 45 or 60 40, I want to
hear from you really about two questions.

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:07.120
Question one is and you can you can let me
know on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.410
Question one is, will he run?

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.030
What do you think?

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.260
Question two.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:17.449
Maybe the more important question is if he
runs.

00:04:17.449 --> 00:04:20.930
What exactly is the path to reelection?

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:27.979
Because I see it as a very, very tough, particularly
when the out party tends to have higher enthusiasm.

00:04:27.979 --> 00:04:32.099
We have this cult of Q Slash Trump, which
is still very, very strong.

00:04:32.099 --> 00:04:40.729
And I think, I mean, listen to there a lot
of the motivation for voting Biden in 2020.

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:43.800
Was to get rid of Donald Trump, that was a
worthy motivation.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.800
I'm not.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.030
That was my motivation.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.370
Among other things, we had to get rid of Trump.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:57.479
With Trump gone, the early signs are it is
tougher to get Democratic voters motivated.

00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:02.270
And so I am worried about Biden's path to
victory in 2024 if he's the candidate.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:05.940
Of course, if he's better than the alternative,
we don't know who that will be.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.620
That might be Trump might be someone else.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.850
I will say we've got to vote for Biden again.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.969
I'm still as pragmatic as ever.

00:05:11.969 --> 00:05:13.779
But I'm curious to hear from you.

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:15.080
Find me on Twitter at De Packman.

